Body:
I would like to point out that the `gpt-5-nano` model is no longer free, so if OpenCode Zen is not configured or does not have any balance, title generation seems to fail as well, depending on what provider/model is being used.

Setting `small_model` in `opencode.jsonc` to any other model, either from a configured provider or to a free Zen model seems to resolve the problem ([docs](https://opencode.ai/docs/config/#models)).

```jsonc
{
    // ...
    "small_model": "qwen3.6-plus-free"
}
```

I don't see the issue here. My local ollama connection works just fine. Problem is that the local models cannot run tools, but the ollama cloud models can for some reason.

My local gemma4 model is not able to use tools and repeatedly asks me what to do. The cloud models works. I also have to add that the cloud model is served via an ollama instance on the same host (my server) and the local gemma runs on my desktop's larger GPU.

<img width="1886" height="780" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f0156e5c-3373-4241-9a67-c54cf24071e8" />

Both are configured the same way

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "edit": "allow",
    "bash": "allow",
    "webfetch": "allow",
    "question": "allow",
    "read": "allow",
    "glob": "allow",
    "write": "allow",
    "task": "allow",
    "todowrite": "allow",
  },
  "provider": {
    "ollama-nas": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "NAS",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "gemma4:31b-cloud": {
          "name": "gemma4:31b-cloud",
          "tools": true
        },
      }
    },
    "ollama-desktop": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "Desktop",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://192.168.184.117:11434/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "gemma4:latest": {
          "name": "gemma4:latest",
          "tools": true
        },
      }
    }

  }
}
```

@kunningKing11 Yeah, it's really weird with the tools calls. I mean why would the cloud models run and not the local ones. They are served by the same API.

I tried verifying if the problem lies in the ollama instance on another machine by adding a cloud model. Again, the cloud model on my desktop works, the local one doesn't

